# Line-ending policy for egl-utils-java — added by ROADMAP item 1.5.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Without it, line endings are a property of each developer's git config
# rather than of the repository, and the toolchain disagrees across platforms:
#
#   Spotless resolves its `lineEndings` from GIT_ATTRIBUTES by default. With no .gitattributes to
#   read it falls back to the PLATFORM's native ending, so on Windows it expects CRLF — while
#   `core.autocrlf=input` had written LF to the working tree. Every line of a file then counts as a
#   format violation: `spotless:check` reported all 77 lines of BuildContractSmokeTest.java as
#   violating on Windows while passing on Linux. Item 1.5's cross-platform format-lint job caught
#   it; before that job existed, format checks only ever ran on Linux, where the accident is benign.
#
# Declaring LF explicitly makes the answer identical for git, Spotless, Checkstyle's
# NewlineAtEndOfFile, and every contributor's editor — regardless of their core.autocrlf setting.

# Default: treat as text, normalise to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Java and build/config sources — LF, stated explicitly rather than relying on the default above.
*.java     text eol=lf
*.xml      text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.sh       text eol=lf
.gitignore   text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf
# .mvn/jvm.config is read line-by-line by the Maven launcher script; keep it LF like every other
# text file, and see .mvn/README.md for the rest of that file's constraints.
jvm.config text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely require CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses LF-terminated batch files.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.cmd      text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.jar      binary
*.zip      binary
*.gz       binary
*.class    binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.gpg      binary
*.keystore binary
